message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SeinePINN_1D: a hybrid LSTM physics-informed neural network for 1-D tidal-river hydrodynamics"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-14
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ranveer82/SeinePINN/tree/SeinePINN_1D"
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Ranveer
    affiliation: "BRGM-French Geological Survey, F-76130 Mont St Aignan, France"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7530-3581"
  - family-names: David
    given-names: Pierre-Yann
    affiliation: "BRGM-French Geological Survey, F-76130 Mont St Aignan, France"
abstract: >-
  SeinePINN_1D reconstructs water level, velocity and discharge along a whole
  tidal river from its boundary forcing alone (upstream discharge, downstream
  stage and tributaries). It couples an LSTM encoder of the forcing with a
  harmonic tidal branch, a hard downstream boundary condition and
  non-dimensional Saint-Venant residuals, and is applied to the 137.7 km Seine
  estuary (France) over 2007-2025 and to a synthetic estuary with a known
  solution.
keywords:
  - physics-informed neural network
  - Saint-Venant equations
  - tidal river
  - estuary
  - hydrodynamics
  - LSTM
  - Seine
